        A support point for generated printers, which are spliced into user modules; not for
        hand-written code. The same holds for `.writeString`, `.writeLong`, `.writeDouble`,
        `.writeBoolean`, `.writeAst`, `.present` and `.writeField`.
    entry .writeString   writes a quoted, escaped JSON string, from generated code
    entry .writeLong   writes an integer, from generated code
    entry .writeDouble   writes a `Double`, from generated code
    entry .writeBoolean   writes `true` or `false`, from generated code
    entry .writeAst   writes a `Json.Ast` tree compactly, from generated code
    entry .present   whether a field's encoded tree is written at all: an absent encoding is omitted
    entry .writeField   writes a field through a nominal `Json.Printable`, from generated code
